  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Institutions pay for smooth operations, trust with families and clean records. They judge you by reliability, courtesy and how you handle pressure.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is keeping a record that someone else could read and use a year later.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and education administration and school management: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft notices, reports and timetables. Routine paperwork shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, integrity and relationships hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and check; later, own decisions and communication.
  </p>

